{
  "$comment": "Language-neutral contract cases. Every SDK replays these against its own HTTP mock and asserts the stated expectations, so identical behavior is enforced by construction rather than by parallel hand-written suites that drift. The error taxonomy itself lives in ../errors.json and is asserted separately; these cases cover behavior that only concrete wire data can express.",
  "version": 2,
  "field_paths": "Dotted, with integer segments indexing into lists: 'choices.0.finish_reason'. A path resolves against the parsed result object, using the SDK's own accessors where it exposes them (for example 'content' and 'usage.total_tokens').",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "chat-completion-basic",
      "operation": "chat.completions.create",
      "request": {
        "model": "qwen3-0-6b-iq4-nl-local-2",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Reply with exactly: hello"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "chat_completion_finished.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "content": "hello",
          "model": "qwen3-0-6b-iq4-nl-local-1",
          "usage.prompt_tokens": 13,
          "usage.completion_tokens": 68,
          "usage.total_tokens": 81,
          "choices.0.finish_reason": "stop"
        }
      },
      "$comment": "Recorded from a live deployment on 2026-09-11. response.model is NOT the requested id: the gateway routes -local-2 to -local-1, so a consumer must never assert that the two match."
    },
    {
      "id": "chat-completion-tool-calls",
      "$comment": "AUTHORED, not recorded: this shape has not been reproduced against a live deployment yet. Tool calls are passed through untouched; the gateway does not interpret them. content is null when the model returns calls instead of prose. The content assertion is withheld: for a null content Python reports None and Go reports \"\", a real divergence tracked as AXO-53 rather than hidden by a lenient runner.",
      "operation": "chat.completions.create",
      "request": {
        "model": "llama3-8b-q4",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "weather in Lima?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "chat_completion_tool_calls.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "choices.0.finish_reason": "tool_calls",
          "tool_calls.0.id": "call_1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "chat-completion-backend-timings",
      "$comment": "Recorded. A reasoning model with a small max_tokens never leaves the reasoning phase: content is empty, finish_reason is length, and there is usage to pay for. Also pins that cache_read is read from the reported prompt_tokens_details rather than derived from timings on this path.",
      "operation": "chat.completions.create",
      "request": {
        "model": "qwen3-0-6b-iq4-nl-local-2",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Say hello"
          }
        ],
        "max_tokens": 24
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "chat_completion.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "content": "",
          "choices.0.finish_reason": "length",
          "timings.predicted_n": 24,
          "timings.cache_n": 9,
          "usage.total_tokens": 34,
          "usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens": 9
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "chat-rate-limit-headers-on-success",
      "$comment": "The budget must be readable before a 429 is ever seen, so a caller can slow down rather than only react.",
      "operation": "chat.completions.create",
      "request": {
        "model": "qwen3-0-6b-iq4-nl-local-2",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Reply with exactly: hello"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "chat_completion_finished.json",
        "headers": {
          "X-Request-ID": "5c1e2b3a-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
          "X-Trace-ID": "b04044d6-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
          "X-RateLimit-Limit-Requests": "60",
          "X-RateLimit-Remaining-Requests": "59",
          "X-RateLimit-Reset-Requests": "1700000060",
          "X-RateLimit-Limit-Tokens": "100000",
          "X-RateLimit-Remaining-Tokens": "99986",
          "X-RateLimit-Reset-Tokens": "1700000060"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "meta.request_id": "5c1e2b3a-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
          "meta.trace_id": "b04044d6-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
          "meta.rate_limit.remaining_requests": 59,
          "meta.rate_limit.remaining_tokens": 99986
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "catalog-list",
      "operation": "models.list",
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "models_catalog.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "data.0.modality": "text",
          "data.1.modality": "text",
          "data.2.modality": "embedding",
          "data.3.modality": "image",
          "data.4.modality": "vision",
          "data.5.modality": "text",
          "data.0.id": "gpt-oss-20b-mxfp4",
          "data.0.context_length": 131072
        }
      },
      "$comment": "Recorded. All four modality values are live; text and vision are BOTH served on the chat endpoint, so the mapping to a consumer's own vocabulary is not one to one."
    },
    {
      "id": "catalog-mine-empty",
      "$comment": "AUTHORED, not recorded: this shape has not been reproduced against a live deployment yet. A token holding an inference scope but no model grants gets an empty list, not an error.",
      "operation": "models.mine",
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "models_mine_empty.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "data": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "catalog-mine-granted",
      "$comment": "Recorded. models.mine() is a strict subset of the public catalog: access is deny-by-default and granted per model, so the catalog answers 'what exists' and this answers 'what may I call'. Note gpt-oss-20b-mxfp4 is in the catalog and absent here.",
      "operation": "models.mine",
      "request": null,
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "models_mine.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "data.0.id": "qwen3-0-6b-iq4-nl-local-2",
          "data.1.id": "qwen3-embedding-0-6b-q8-0-local",
          "data.2.id": "sd-turbo-test",
          "data.3.id": "qwen3vl-8b-q4"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "embeddings-batch",
      "$comment": "Recorded. completion_tokens is absent because there is no generation phase -- not zero.",
      "operation": "embeddings.create",
      "request": {
        "model": "qwen3-embedding-0-6b-q8-0-local",
        "input": [
          "first text",
          "second text"
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "embeddings.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "data.0.index": 0,
          "data.1.index": 1,
          "usage.prompt_tokens": 6,
          "usage.completion_tokens": null
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "images-base64",
      "$comment": "AUTHORED, not recorded: this shape has not been reproduced against a live deployment yet. Images come back inline as base64, never as a URL; decoding and persisting is the caller's job.",
      "operation": "images.generate",
      "request": {
        "model": "sd-turbo",
        "prompt": "a photo of a cat",
        "n": 1,
        "size": "512x512"
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body_file": "images.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "ok",
        "fields": {
          "output_format": "png",
          "data.0.b64_json": "aVZCT1J3MEtHZ28="
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "stream-basic",
      "$comment": "Recorded. Ends with [DONE] TWICE -- the backend sends one and the gateway appends its own -- so a client must stop at the first. No usage chunk arrives at all, so the counts come from the final chunk's timings and are flagged estimated.",
      "operation": "chat.completions.stream",
      "request": {
        "model": "qwen3-0-6b-iq4-nl-local-2",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Count 1 2 3"
          }
        ],
        "max_tokens": 24
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "sse_file": "chat_stream_ok.sse"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "stream",
        "content": "",
        "chunks": 24,
        "usage": {
          "prompt_tokens": 15,
          "completion_tokens": 24,
          "cache_read_tokens": 14,
          "estimated": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "stream-usage-chunk",
      "$comment": "AUTHORED, not recorded: this shape has not been reproduced against a live deployment yet. Backends that do report usage take precedence over any figure derived from timings.",
      "operation": "chat.completions.stream",
      "request": {
        "model": "m",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Hi"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "sse_file": "chat_stream_usage.sse"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "stream",
        "content": "Hi",
        "chunks": 2,
        "usage": {
          "prompt_tokens": 5,
          "completion_tokens": 9,
          "estimated": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "stream-terminates-immediately",
      "operation": "chat.completions.stream",
      "request": {
        "model": "m",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Hi"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "sse_file": "chat_stream_empty.sse"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "stream",
        "content": "",
        "chunks": 0,
        "usage": null
      },
      "$comment": "AUTHORED, not recorded: this shape has not been reproduced against a live deployment yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "stream-interrupted",
      "$comment": "AUTHORED, not recorded: this shape has not been reproduced against a live deployment yet. The status is 200 and the headers are already committed, so only the in-band chunk reveals the failure. Detection must key off the presence of an 'error' field rather than its message. The partial output received first must survive on the raised error.",
      "operation": "chat.completions.stream",
      "request": {
        "model": "m",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Hi"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "sse_file": "chat_stream_interrupted.sse"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "stream_error",
        "error": "stream-interrupted",
        "partial_content": "Hello, wor"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "error-unknown-model",
      "$comment": "Recorded from a live deployment on 2026-09-11.",
      "operation": "chat.completions.create",
      "request": {
        "model": "no-existe",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "x"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 400,
        "body_file": "err_unknown_model.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "error",
        "error_type_suffix": "unknown-model",
        "retryable": false,
        "has_request_id": true,
        "has_trace_id": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "error-forbidden-missing-model-scope",
